<title>USA: Digital calls Intel suit a &quot;diversion&quot;.</title>
<headline>Digital calls Intel suit a &quot;diversion&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>MAYNARD, Mass. 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Digital Equipment Corp said Wednesday that Intel Corp's countersuit against the company is a diversion from the central issues of Digital's patent infringement against Intel.</p>
<p>In a written statement, Digital general counsel Thomas Siekman said Intel's suit &quot;is without merit and unjustified.&quot; Digital had anticipated the action, he said.</p>
<p>The Intel suit followed a suit filed on May 12 by Digital in U.S. District Court. In its suit, Digital charged Intel with infringement of 10 Digital patents in production of Intel's Pentium, Pentium Pro and Pentium II microprocessors.</p>
</text>
